> Yes I have only a single SC008 chassis. How do I configure it to be
> 2 4 port units?

> The unit is marked as follows:
> Left:
> transmit
> 0 to 3 have terminators, 4 to 7 are unconnected TNC's

> Right:
> receive
> 0 to 3 have terminators, 4 to 7 are unconnected TNC's

> Middle:
> 1 is patched to 4
> 2 is patched to 5
> 3 and 6 are unconnected and have no terminators.

> Can you detail the A and B port Tx and Rx connections, as 2 4 port
> units?

The terminators are 50 ohm, and the cable is ethernet cable, but blue
and with TNCs on the end. For a short run, *GOOD* 50 ohm coax can be
used. Dont even think of trying to put BNCs in there though. Thinnet
coax with TNCs will do. If you can get the DEC speced Belden, that is
the best of them.

EK-SC008-UG does not have a conectivity diagram :( The 8 port config
requires the top jumper, the one from 1 to 4. But all the pictures
show 2 jumpers, 1-4 and 2-5. I'm wondering if there was a change in
SC008s at some time... I'll see if I can find another info source.

It is all transformers, so you can't use a meter to trace the
connections.

