John Forkosh wrote:
> 
> I have a couple of these in a vs4000/90, one as on "online backup"
> that I'd rather not spin up until I actually mount it, since they
> run kind of hot.  I have the seagate docs for the drive, and have
> tried jumpering the "delay motor start" and "enable motor start"
> jumpers, but the drive always spins up at power on.  How can I get
> it to stop doing that?  Thanks,

FWIW:

The VS4000/90 does not automatically issue a start command to drives. 
It WILL issue one if you use the console command SHOW DEVICE.  In
particular, SHOW CONFIG does not start the drive.

If you are using VMS, it does not start the drive until you access it,
either with MOUNT or INIT.

The correct way to jumper the drive is to disable both "delay" and
"start". "delay" starts the drive after some number of seconds times the
SCSI ID, so if the drive is jumpered to ID 0, it starts immediately.

Good luck!

