Some drives enable an option when the jumper is present, some disable
it.  You need to check the manual for the particular drive.
 
According to Seagate's manual for the ST15150N, page 41, found at:

http://www.seagate.com/support/disc/iguides/scsi/28870e.pdf

you want to have the MTR jumper on.  This causes the drive to wait for a
START UNIT command.

If you want to determine whether the drive is spinning itself up or if
it is being commanded to spin up, try disconnecting the SCSI cable. 
Then power it up.  If it spins up on its own, you know it is the drive. 
(NOTE: This does not work with all drives.  Some drives don't initialize
correctly if they don't find a validly terminated SCSI bus.)

Good luck!

