Did you FTP the files? You need to specify ASCII here instead of BINARY to
get them converted from one OS format to the other.

One other thing to check is if the files were initially readable in the
middle, on the VAX. If the problem started there, edit the file with TECO,
and immediately do an ex<esc><esc> and TECO will convert the PDP-11 file
format to native VMS. Then do the ASCII FTP from the VMS system to your PC.
I've used this little TECO trick many times to fix ASCII files with messed
up formats.

