  A form-feed is whitespace, and appears entirely legal within a C source
  file per my reading of the C materials.  Large tracts of OpenVMS source
  code certainly use form-feed characters embedded within the source
  files; OpenVMS uses form-feeds for purposes of readability.

  For those interested, the first couple of pages of the lexicon chapter of
  the OpenVMS C Language Reference Manual have various relevent details.

    http://www.hp.com/go/openvms/doc/

	-=-

  The discussion of file transfers over to Microsoft Windows systems almost
  certainly involves a need to switch the sequential files to Stream or to
  Stream LF format -- before moving the files along to the Windows platforms.
  OpenVMS has a number of sequential file formats and record organizations,
  and only a select few combinations are compatible with the Microsoft
  sequential file formats and expectations.

