"alphadoc" <all.the.fun@the.fair> writes:


> How do I connect my HSJ50 and my CIPCA to the star coupler?  I am
> sure that the process is straight forward, but I am asking just to
> be sure I have it right.

First, the CI is totally duplicated, A and B are identical,
independant IO systems almost.

For each of A and B, Connect all the xmit cables to one side of the
SC.  Then connect all the receive cables to the other side. Rince and
repeat for the other path. Or not if you only have one.  The SC is a
set of 2-1 xformers aranged as a dual fan. One lot to combine the
signals into one, the other side splits it out to each receiver.

With a HSC50, you will not be able to run large packets and the new
arbitration scheme, so be sure that the CIPCA is set to the old
standard. It has probably been set to the newer protocol stuff. It is
in the good book.  I think you will also need to be sure the HSC50
Link module is up to rev for a CIPCA.

