Well I always worked in MCR mode, so for me that would have been PIP 
/FR ddnn:.  That won't show whether the space is contiguous or not 
tho'. If the ...CA. catch-all task is running then FRE ddnn: might 
give you the same answer.

If you are short of contiguous space, it is most probably due to .TSK 
files,so you could try copying those files that must be contiguous 
first. .TSK files _must_ be contiguous (IIRC). A little voice in my 
head says something about .OLB's too but I'm not so sure. Our last 
pdp-11/60 died 2 years ago now.

To recover contiguous space, check out Disk Save and Compress (DSC) 
and/or BRU utilities.

-- 
Cheers - Dave.


