I found a CI cable in my box of ancient stuff.

The part number is BNCI-10 (10 meters).  Or 17-01551-01 Rev. C01.  Or
36-24502-01 Rev B01.

This is definitely NOT RG58-A/U cable.  The jacket is blue (like all CI
cables I have seen), it is fairly stiff, and it appears to have an extra
layer of braided sheilding.  The markings on the cable are: NEK CABLE  
...  125C ... 16 AWG ... (UL) Type CL2P  ...  FT6.

I think this cable was never used.  It it is rolled in a spool with a
diameter of about 4 inches.  This is definitely the thinner of the two
kinds of CI cable I have seen.

